# The bull shark in the game, frame by frame (2026-11-22, CLAUDE.md's hard rule: every clip filmed in the real game,
# frozen and stepped, from three sides): every clip on a still shark named film:<clip> (it plays only that clip). The
# deep-water clips in the open air a block over the grass (a still film shark does not fall, and through a tank's glass
# the three-quarter camera saw only glass); the prowl, the breach and the spy hop in a glass tank of water 5 deep at its
# surface (the water at the prowl's waterline, 24.5 model pixels over its feet); the beached flop on the grass beside the
# tank; then a small shark and a big scarred one side by side. Each burst covers the whole clip, side on, three quarters
# from the front and above, and from the front.
#   ./gradlew runFilm -PfilmScene=tools/film/bull_shark_frames.film   pictures in run-film/screenshots/bull_shark_frames/
cmd time set noon
cmd weather clear
cmd kill @e[type=!player]
cmd fill -2 -61 -6 16 -50 6 minecraft:air
cmd fill 0 -61 -4 14 -56 4 minecraft:glass
cmd fill 1 -60 -3 13 -56 3 minecraft:water
lens 50
wait 40
cmd summon antcolonies:bull_shark 46.0 -59.00 0.5 {NoAI:1b,Length:5.5f,Rotation:[-90f,0f],CustomName:'"film:idle"'}
camera 46.00 -59.82 -12.50 0 2
wait 10
cmd tick freeze
burst idle_side 12 5
cmd tick unfreeze
cmd tp @e[type=antcolonies:bull_shark] 7 -140 0
wait 3
cmd summon antcolonies:bull_shark 46.0 -59.00 0.5 {NoAI:1b,Length:5.5f,Rotation:[-90f,0f],CustomName:'"film:idle"'}
camera 54.50 -56.12 -8.50 45 18
